# Plan: DropUI React port (`drop-ui-react`)

> Revised 2026-10-06 against commit `ef0cebe` ("merge accessibility work into bundle-size branch"). The previous revision covered the app up to `6d34233` ("values are state"). Three changes have landed since: inline spans (`3a7a89f`), the bundle-size pass (`96b1a4e`) and the accessibility pass (`b13d11e`), which added a keyboard alternative to drag & drop, user-facing element labels, screen reader announcements, focus management, dialog labelling and reduced-motion handling.

## Context

DropUI is an Angular 22 drag & drop UI builder. The persistence plans next to this file already say the app will be ported to other frameworks as separate projects sharing one backend. This plan covers the React port.

Decisions made with the user:

- **Location:** a new sibling repo, `C:\Users\telis\Repos\drop-ui-react`. The Angular repo is not modified.
- **State:** Zustand.

Goal: feature parity with the Angular app at `ef0cebe`, proven by the same three test suites. The six Playwright files in `drop-ui/e2e/` (42 tests) are the acceptance contract: they are copied over and must pass without changes to their assertions.

