## Stores

ADR 0001 is the specification for both stores. Its rules carry over one for one; only the mechanism changes.

| ADR 0001 rule | SignalStore | Zustand |
|---|---|---|
| One store per feature, provided in root | `signalStore({ providedIn: 'root' })` | `createBuilderStore()` / `createThemeStore()` factories, one instance each, held in a context provider at the app root |
| Components inject the store and read signals | `inject(BuilderStore)` | `useBuilderStore(selector)` / `useThemeStore(selector)` |
| Components never change state themselves | protected state | the hooks expose only selected state and actions; `setState` is not exported |
| Each method is one atomic update | `patchState(store, fn)` | `set((state) => ...)`; the updater bodies copy unchanged |
| The store owns its invariants | guards inside methods | same guards (`Number.isFinite`, `clampGridSize`, `THEMES.includes`, `'text' in element`, `'value' in element`, `type === 'dropdown'`, `hasOption`, unknown `uid`) |
| Derived data is never stored | `withComputed` | exported pure selector + memoizing hook |
| Pure helpers above the store | module functions | copied unchanged: `createElement`, `hasOption`, `selectedValue`, `insertIntoCell`, `clampGridSize`, `isInCell`, `positionInCell`, `countOf`, `CELL_AXIS`, `createInitialState` |
| Side effects in `withHooks` | `effect()` in `onInit` | `store.subscribe(...)` inside the factory |
| The store announces its own changes | `inject(LiveAnnouncer)` as a `withMethods` default argument | an `announce(message)` function passed to the factory |
| Stores do not inject each other | — | same; a component that needs both uses both hooks |

### Announcements

The Angular stores, not the components, announce canvas and theme changes, so a drag and its keyboard alternative report the same outcome. Keep that: no component calls the announcer.

- `shared/announcer/announcer.ts` exports `createAnnouncer(document = window.document)`, returning `announce(message: string): void`. It appends one `<div class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">` to `<body>` on first use and writes the message as its text. Clear the text before setting it so the same message twice in a row is spoken twice, which is what CDK's `LiveAnnouncer` does.
- One announcer is created in `main.tsx` and passed to both factories: `createBuilderStore({ announce, initial? })`, `createThemeStore({ announce, document? })`.
- Store specs pass `vi.fn()` and assert on it, replacing `vi.spyOn(TestBed.inject(LiveAnnouncer), 'announce')`. The e2e suite asserts the region's text with `getByText(...).toBeAttached()`, so the region has to stay in the DOM and must not be `hidden`.
- dnd-kit ships its own live region with "picked up / dropped" messages. Silence it (`accessibility.announcements` on `DndContext` returning nothing), or the store's message competes with it.

### `BuilderStore`

Port `drop-ui/src/app/features/builder/state/builder-store.ts` nearly line for line.

- Actions: `setGridSize(axis, size)`, `addElement`, `updateText`, `updateOptions`, `updateValue`, `removeElement`, `moveElement`. `updateOptions` also keeps the dropdown selection valid through the `selectedValue` helper.
- Palette labels come from `ELEMENT_LABELS` in `palette-item.ts`: the div is "Block text" and the span is "Inline text". Every user-facing name of an element type (palette, actions button, announcements) reads from that record.
- `removeElement` and `moveElement` now look the element up first and return silently for an unknown `uid`. In Zustand: read with `get()`, call `set(...)`, read `get()` again for the announcement.
- What each action announces, exactly as the specs and `keyboard.e2e.ts` expect:

| Action | Message | Silent when |
|---|---|---|
| `addElement` | `{item.label} added to {cellLabel(cell)}.` | never |
| `moveElement` to another cell | `{label} moved to {cellLabel(cell)}.` | unknown `uid` |
| `moveElement` within its cell | `{label} moved to position {n} of {count}.` | the position did not change |
| `removeElement` | `{label} deleted.` | unknown `uid` |
| `setGridSize` | `Grid set to {countOf(rows, 'row')} and {countOf(columns, 'column')}.`, read after clamping | the size is not finite |

- `createElement` keeps its exhaustive `switch` with no `default` branch (ADR 0002 rule 4).
- `cells` → exported pure `selectCells(grid, canvasElements): GridCell[]` plus a `useCells()` hook that selects `grid` and `canvasElements` separately and derives with `useMemo`. Do not return a freshly built array from a Zustand selector: in v5 that re-renders forever.
- `initial?: Partial<BuilderState>` takes preset state so tests can mount a component against a known canvas, the equivalent of stubbing `BuilderStore` in `providers`.

### `ThemeStore`

Port `drop-ui/src/app/features/theme/state/theme-store.ts`.

- `THEMES` (from `daisyui/functions/themeOrder`) and `createInitialState(root)` copy unchanged. There is no default-theme constant: the starting theme is read from `data-theme` on `<html>`, and a missing or unknown name falls back to `THEMES[0]` with `allThemesRequested: true`.
- State is `{ theme, allThemesRequested }`. `loadAllThemes()` sets the flag; `setTheme` ignores names that are not in `THEMES` and otherwise sets the theme and the flag and announces `Theme changed to {theme}.`
- The two `withHooks` effects become: the factory writes `data-theme` once and then on every change through `store.subscribe`, and appends `<link rel="stylesheet" href="themes.css">` to `<head>` the first time `allThemesRequested` is true. The attribute goes on `<html>`, not on the shell, so Base UI portals under `<body>` are themed too (`theme.e2e.ts`: "a picked theme also restyles overlays rendered outside the app root").
- `index.html` is the only place that names the default theme: `data-theme="fantasy"` on `<html>` and a `<link>` to `themes/fantasy.css`, so the first paint is themed before the store exists. `styles.css` builds no theme.
- `ThemePicker` calls `loadAllThemes()` when its menu opens (`theme.e2e.ts`: "loads the other themes when the theme list is opened").

