## Verification

In `drop-ui-react`:

1. `npm run build` (type check + production build) passes. Check the CSS output for daisyUI components the app does not use (tabs, steps, table): their presence means source detection is scanning too much.
2. `npm test -- --watch=false`, `npm run test:components -- --watch=false`, `npm run e2e` all green.
3. Manual pass on `npm run dev`:
   - Grid: set 2×2; type "12" into rows and confirm the grid does not collapse mid-typing; shrink to 1×1 and confirm no element is lost.
   - Drag: drop each of the six element types into cells, reorder within a cell, move across cells. Two spans sit on one line; a div takes its own.
   - Form controls: type into a dropped text input and pick a date without the element starting to drag; drag the same element by its wrapper to another cell and confirm the value is still there.
   - Edit text on a div and on a text input (placeholder changes); Save disabled when blank.
   - Dropdown: add two options, delete one (focus moves to the previous row), save, reopen and confirm the rows are still there.
   - Delete with cancel and with confirm.
   - Theme: open the picker (current theme is checked, focused and in view), pick `dracula`, confirm the header, canvas and an open menu or dialog all restyle.
   - Keyboard only, mouse unplugged: Tab to the palette, add an element to a chosen cell, move it earlier and later, move it to another cell, edit it, delete it. After every step focus is somewhere sensible (the table under "Keyboard alternative and focus") and never on `<body>`.
   - Screen reader (NVDA or Narrator): each add, move, delete, grid change and theme change is spoken once, with the same wording for a drag as for its menu alternative; dialogs read their title and description on open.
   - Reduced motion (DevTools → Rendering → emulate `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`): a dropped element lands at once, with no slide.
4. Side by side with the Angular app on port 4200: same roles, names and behaviour for each step above.
